{% doc %}
  "להשלים את הערכה" inside the cart — accessories that fit what is already in it.

  The shell only, and it starts hidden: the tiles come from sections/cart-upsell rendered against
  /search and fetched by assets/cart-upsell.js, and a block that may legitimately come back empty
  should not hold space in a drawer while it waits. No skeleton for the same reason.

  The anchor is the first line that is a device (type מכשירים, טאבלטים, שעונים or אוזניות),
  because that is what the rest of the cart hangs off: someone buying a phone still needs a case,
  someone buying a case does not need another one, and a game or a gift card has no accessories to
  match. A cart with no device in it gets no block at all.

  Every query names the model or the maker. One that would be the group word alone ("כבל", "כיסוי")
  is not sent: it would fill the row with whatever ranks first in the whole catalogue. The house
  vendor ("joy mobile", the store itself on 236 products) is no maker, so it counts as none.

  @param {string} [context] - 'drawer' (default) or 'page'; picks the layout.

  @example
  {% render 'cart-upsell', context: 'drawer' %}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign cu_context = context | default: 'drawer'
  assign cu_anchor = nil
  assign cu_skip = ''

  for cu_line in cart.items
    assign cu_skip = cu_skip | append: cu_line.product.handle | append: ','
    if cu_anchor == nil
      assign cu_line_type = cu_line.product.type | strip
      case cu_line_type
        when 'מכשירים', 'טאבלטים', 'שעונים', 'אוזניות'
          assign cu_anchor = cu_line.product
      endcase
    endif
  endfor
-%}

{%- if cu_anchor != nil -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Two queries, not every group: the cart is not the place to browse a catalogue. They are the
    first two groups of snippets/addon-groups (the same rules as the product page) that name a model
    or a brand; a group that would ask for its word alone ("כבל", "מטען") is skipped, because it
    would fill the row with whatever ranks first in the whole catalogue.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- capture cu_groups -%}{%- render 'addon-groups', product: cu_anchor -%}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign cu_queries = ''
    assign cu_taken = 0
    assign cu_list = cu_groups | strip | remove_first: '###' | split: '###'
    for cu_group in cu_list
      if cu_taken >= 2
        break
      endif
      assign cu_parts = cu_group | split: '|'
      assign cu_prefix = cu_parts[0] | append: '|' | append: cu_parts[1] | append: '|'
      assign cu_query = cu_group | remove_first: cu_prefix | strip
      assign cu_word = cu_parts[1] | strip
      if cu_query == blank or cu_query == cu_word
        continue
      endif
      if cu_queries != blank
        assign cu_queries = cu_queries | append: '|||'
      endif
      assign cu_queries = cu_queries | append: cu_query
      assign cu_taken = cu_taken | plus: 1
    endfor
  -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    The stylesheet and the script are loaded by the calling section, not here: this markup reaches
    the page through section rendering after a cart change, and a <script> inserted that way never
    executes — a cart that started empty would print the block and leave it hidden forever.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if cu_queries != blank -%}
    <cart-upsell
      class="cu cu--{{ cu_context }}"
      data-cu-queries="{{ cu_queries | escape }}"
      data-cu-skip="{{ cu_skip | escape }}"
      data-cu-limit="4"
      data-cu-str-error="{{ 'cart.upsell.error' | t | escape }}"
      data-cu-str-added="{{ 'cart.upsell.added' | t | escape }}"
      hidden
    >
      <div class="cu__head">
        <h2 class="cu__heading">{{ 'cart.upsell.heading' | t }}</h2>
        <p class="cu__sub">{{ 'cart.upsell.sub' | t }}</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="cu__list" role="list" data-cu-list></ul>
    </cart-upsell>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
